      </table>
      <h3 class="Cite" id="10.70.10.040"><a name="10.70.10.040">10-70.10.040</a> Additional Standards</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="bold">Ancillary Structure Standards. </span>All ancillary structures within parks and common space, including, but not limited to, open-air pavilions, gazebos, picnic shelters and outdoor theaters, shall not be subject to the physical requirements of the building form standards in Chapter <a href="../Flagstaff10/Flagstaff1040000.html#10.40">10-40</a>, Specific to Zones. They shall be designed and furnished to be consistent with the character of the zone in which they are located. Such consistency may require ancillary structures to maintain building setbacks, frontage, massing, disposition and character similar to adjacent development as determined by the Director.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="bold">Civic Building Standards.</span> Civic buildings located in larger parks and common spaces including but not limited to community centers, meeting rooms, public safety facilities, houses of worship and schools, shall not be subject to the physical requirements of the building form standards in Chapter <a href="../Flagstaff10/Flagstaff1040040.html#10.40.40">10-40.40</a>, Transect Zones. They shall be designed and furnished to be consistent with the character of the zone in which they are located. Such consistency may require ancillary structures to maintain building setbacks, frontage, massing, location and character similar to adjacent development.</p>

            <p class="HistoryNote">(Ord. 2023-29, Amended, 12/5/2023 (Res. 2023-58))</p>

